# Copy this file to .env.local and adjust for the current machine.
# Keep .env.local untracked.
#
# This file is for non-secret machine configuration: paths, environment names,
# and data roots. Keep credentials out of it. Makefile includes .env.local and
# exports its variables, so every value here reaches the environment of every
# command a make target runs, and everything those commands spawn. Store API
# keys, tokens, and passwords with the tool's own login command, a credential
# helper, a system keychain, or a secret manager. See docs/local-development.md.

# Add project-specific variables as needed. Examples:
# PROJECT_ENV=          # conda or virtualenv name
# PROJECT_PYTHON=       # path to the python interpreter
# PROJECT_EXTERNAL_DATA_ROOT=  # Box, Drive, raw-data, private-data, or other external root used by _data/
# PROJECT_ASSET_ROOT=   # path to a local asset or media root

# Template source clone used when checking for newer template changes.
# PROJECT_TEMPLATE_REPO=  # path to the local clone of this template repository

# Related repository clone paths. These are machine-specific and should be
# mirrored with ignored symlinks under _repos/ when the project needs
# cross-repo context.
#
# For each related repository, define one project-specific path variable. Then
# list the _repos/ link name and variable name in PROJECT_RELATED_REPOS so
# `make setup` can create or refresh the local symlink.
# PROJECT_EXAMPLE_REPO=       # path to a related repository clone
# PROJECT_RELATED_REPOS=example:PROJECT_EXAMPLE_REPO

# Optional PDF and office-document tooling. Fill these when the project needs
# local PDF inspection, PDF-to-image/text conversion, or document/spreadsheet
# conversion.
# PROJECT_POPPLER_BIN=       # directory containing Poppler CLI tools, such as pdfinfo and pdftoppm
# PROJECT_PDFINFO=           # path to the Poppler pdfinfo executable
# PROJECT_SOFFICE=           # path to LibreOffice soffice for document/spreadsheet conversion
# PROJECT_LIBREOFFICE_APP=   # path to the macOS LibreOffice app bundle

# The examples below are illustrations of the variable format, not defaults.
# This template was first developed on macOS, so the macOS paths came first.
# Resolve the real locations with `command -v pdfinfo` and `command -v soffice`
# before copying any value into .env.local.

# Apple Silicon macOS with Homebrew. Intel Homebrew uses /usr/local/bin.
# PROJECT_POPPLER_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin
# PROJECT_PDFINFO=/opt/homebrew/bin/pdfinfo
# PROJECT_SOFFICE=/opt/homebrew/bin/soffice
# PROJECT_LIBREOFFICE_APP=/Applications/LibreOffice.app

# Linux, including shared compute clusters. Paths depend on the system package
# manager, conda environment, or environment module in use.
# PROJECT_LIBREOFFICE_APP applies only to macOS and should be left unset here.
# PROJECT_POPPLER_BIN=/usr/bin
# PROJECT_PDFINFO=/usr/bin/pdfinfo
# PROJECT_SOFFICE=/usr/bin/soffice
